      <h2>Building Sustainable Habits</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>Why Everyday Recycling Matters</h3>

        <figure>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532996122724-e3c354a0b15b?w=300&h=200&fit=crop"
            alt="Coloured recycling bins for sorting plastic, paper, and glass"
            width="300"
            height="200"
          >
          <figcaption>
            Proper sorting of plastic, paper, and organic waste protects local ecosystems.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Small recycling adjustments in our daily routines drastically reduce landfill waste. 
          By taking a moment to separate glass, paper, and plastics, we preserve raw natural resources.
        </p>

        <p>
          Learn more about local recycling guidelines here:
          <a href="https://www.epa.gov/recycle" target="_blank">
            EPA Recycling Guide
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Smart Plastic Alternatives</h3>

        <figure>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1605647540924-852290f6b0d5?w=300&h=200&fit=crop"
            alt="A reusable canvas tote bag alongside bamboo toothbrushes"
            width="300"
            height="200"
          >
          <figcaption>
            Switching to reusable canvas bags and bamboo products lowers your daily carbon footprint.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Single-use plastics take hundreds of years to break down in our oceans and soil. 
          Swapping out plastic grocery bags for canvas totes and choosing metal straws helps heal the earth.
        </p>

        <p>
          Explore more sustainability facts here:
          <a href="https://www.unep.org/" target="_blank">
            UN Environment Programme
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section id="green-tips">
      <h2>Green Tips for Students</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>Conserve Energy in Your Room</h3>

        <p>
          Unplugging device chargers when they aren't actively in use prevents "vampire" power draw. 
          Turning off overhead lights when leaving your room is an easy way to save electricity.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Switch to Refillable Bottles</h3>

        <p>
          Carrying a reusable stainless steel water bottle eliminates reliance on single-use bottles. 
          It keeps plastic out of the environment and keeps your drinks colder for longer.
        </p>

        <p>
          Read more about student climate action here:
          <a href="https://www.climaterealityproject.org/" target="_blank">
            Climate Reality Project
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

